{"id":"CVE-2022-2237","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2023-03-27T00:00:00.000Z","updated":"2025-02-24T19:15:29.345Z","description":"A flaw was found in the Keycloak Node.js Adapter. This flaw allows an attacker to benefit from an Open Redirect vulnerability in the checkSso function.","cwe":["CWE-601 CWE-601"],"metrics":[{"src":"CISA-ADP","v":"3.1","score":6.1,"sev":"MEDIUM","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:C/C:L/I:L/A:N"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"none","Automatable":"no","Technical Impact":"partial"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"Keycloak","versions":["affected unknown"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2097007"}],"vendors":["nodejs"]}
{"id":"CVE-2022-21824","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"hackerone","published":"2022-02-24T00:00:00.000Z","updated":"2025-04-30T22:24:41.602Z","description":"Due to the formatting logic of the \"console.table()\" function it was not safe to allow user controlled input to be passed to the \"properties\" parameter while simultaneously passing a plain object with at least one property as the first parameter, which could be \"__proto__\". The prototype pollution has very limited control, in that it only allows an empty string to be assigned to numerical keys of the object prototype.Node.js >= 12.22.9, >= 14.18.3, >= 16.13.2, and >= 17.3.1 use a null protoype for the object these properties are being assigned to.","cwe":["CWE-471 Modification of Assumed-Immutable Data (MAID) (CWE-471)"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"NodeJS","product":"Node","defaultStatus":"unaffected","versions":["affected 4.0 <4.* (semver)","affected 5.0 <5.* (semver)","affected 6.0 <6.* (semver)","affected 7.0 <7.* (semver)","affected 8.0 <8.* (semver)","affected 9.0 <9.* (semver)","affected 10.0 <10.* (semver)","affected 11.0 <11.* (semver)","affected 12.0 <12.22.9 (semver)","affected 13.0 <13.* (semver)","affected 14.0 <14.18.3 (semver)","affected 15.0 <15.* (semver)","affected 16.0 <16.13.2 (semver)","affected 17.0 <17.3.1 (semver)"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://nodejs.org/en/blog/vulnerability/jan-2022-security-releases/"},{"url":"https://hackerone.com/reports/1431042"},{"url":"https://www.oracle.com/security-alerts/cpuapr2022.html"},{"url":"https://security.netapp.com/advisory/ntap-20220325-0007/"},{"url":"https://www.debian.org/security/2022/dsa-5170","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"DSA-5170"},{"url":"https://www.oracle.com/security-alerts/cpujul2022.html"},{"url":"https://security.netapp.com/advisory/ntap-20220729-0004/"},{"url":"https://lists.debian.org/debian-lts-announce/2022/10/msg00006.html","tags":["mailing-list"],"name":"[debian-lts-announce] 20221005 [SECURITY] [DLA 3137-1] nodejs security update"}],"vendors":["nodejs"]}
{"id":"CVE-2022-27780","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"hackerone","published":"2022-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","updated":"2026-10-14T16:20:10.291Z","description":"The curl URL parser wrongly accepts percent-encoded URL separators like '/'when decoding the host name part of a URL, making it a *different* URL usingthe wrong host name when it is later retrieved.For example, a URL like `http://example.com%2F127.0.0.1/`, would be allowed bythe parser and get transposed into `http://example.com/127.0.0.1/`. This flawcan be used to circumvent filters, checks and more.","cwe":["CWE-177 Improper Handling of URL Encoding (Hex Encoding) (CWE-177)"],"metrics":[{"src":"CISA-ADP","v":"3.1","score":5.3,"sev":"MEDIUM","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:N"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"poc","Automatable":"yes","Technical Impact":"partial"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"https://github.com/curl/curl","versions":["affected Fixed in 7.83.1"]},{"vendor":"haxx","product":"curl","defaultStatus":"unknown","cpes":["cpe:2.3:a:haxx:curl:*:*:*:*:*:*:*:*"],"versions":["affected 0 <7.86.0 (custom)"]},{"vendor":"netapp","product":"solidfire_\\&_hci_storage_node","defaultStatus":"unknown","cpes":["cpe:2.3:a:netapp:solidfire_\\&_hci_storage_node:*:*:*:*:*:*:*:*"],"versions":["affected 0"]},{"vendor":"netapp","product":"ontap_9","defaultStatus":"unknown","cpes":["cpe:2.3:a:netapp:ontap_9:*:*:*:*:*:*:*:*"],"versions":["affected 0"]},{"vendor":"netapp","product":"solidfire_\\&_hci_management_node","defaultStatus":"unknown","cpes":["cpe:2.3:a:netapp:hci_baseboard_management_controller:h300s:*:*:*:*:*:*:*","cpe:2.3:a:netapp:hci_baseboard_management_controller:h410s:*:*:*:*:*:*:*","cpe:2.3:a:netapp:hci_baseboard_management_controller:h500s:*:*:*:*:*:*:*","cpe:2.3:a:netapp:hci_baseboard_management_controller:h700s:*:*:*:*:*:*:*"],"versions":["affected h300s","affected h410s","affected h500s","affected h700s"]},{"vendor":"netapp","product":"hci_bootstrap_os","defaultStatus":"unknown","cpes":["cpe:2.3:o:netapp:hci_bootstrap_os:*:*:*:*:*:*:*:*"],"versions":["affected 0"]},{"vendor":"netapp","product":"solidfire_\\&_hci_management_node","defaultStatus":"unknown","cpes":["cpe:2.3:a:netapp:solidfire_\\&_hci_management_node:*:*:*:*:*:*:*:*"],"versions":["affected 0"]},{"vendor":"Siemens","product":"SIMATIC S7-1500 CPU 1518-4 PN/DP MFP","defaultStatus":"unknown","versions":["affected V3.1.0 <V3.1.5 (custom)"]},{"vendor":"Siemens","product":"SIMATIC S7-1500 CPU 1518F-4 PN/DP MFP","defaultStatus":"unknown","versions":["affected V3.1.0 <V3.1.5 (custom)"]},{"vendor":"Siemens","product":"SIPLUS S7-1500 CPU 1518-4 PN/DP MFP","defaultStatus":"unknown","versions":["affected V3.1.0 <V3.1.5 (custom)"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://hackerone.com/reports/1553841"},{"url":"https://security.netapp.com/advisory/ntap-20220609-0009/"},{"url":"https://security.gentoo.org/glsa/202212-01","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"GLSA-202212-01"},{"url":"https://cert-portal.siemens.com/productcert/html/ssa-398330.html"}],"vendors":["curl","nodejs"]}
{"id":"CVE-2022-29078","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2022-04-25T14:13:32.000Z","updated":"2024-08-03T06:10:58.967Z","description":"The ejs (aka Embedded JavaScript templates) package 3.1.6 for Node.js allows server-side template injection in settings[view options][outputFunctionName]. This is parsed as an internal option, and overwrites the outputFunctionName option with an arbitrary OS command (which is executed upon template compilation).","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/mde/ejs/releases","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://eslam.io/posts/ejs-server-side-template-injection-rce/","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://security.netapp.com/advisory/ntap-20220804-0001/","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]}],"vendors":["nodejs"]}
{"id":"CVE-2022-29080","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2022-04-12T04:45:34.000Z","updated":"2024-08-03T06:10:59.380Z","description":"The npm-dependency-versions package through 0.3.0 for Node.js allows command injection if an attacker is able to call dependencyVersions with a JSON object in which pkgs is a key, and there are shell metacharacters in a value.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/barneycarroll/npm-dependency-versions/issues/6","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://www.npmjs.com/package/npm-dependency-versions","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]}],"vendors":["nodejs"]}
{"id":"CVE-2022-30241","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2022-05-04T17:29:55.000Z","updated":"2024-08-03T06:40:47.892Z","description":"The jquery.json-viewer library through 1.4.0 for Node.js does not properly escape characters such as < in a JSON object, as demonstrated by a SCRIPT element.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/abodelot/jquery.json-viewer/pull/26","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://www.npmjs.com/package/jquery.json-viewer","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]}],"vendors":["nodejs"]}
{"id":"CVE-2022-31150","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"GitHub_M","published":"2022-07-19T20:40:10.000Z","updated":"2025-04-22T17:48:45.328Z","title":"CRLF injection in request headers","description":"undici is an HTTP/1.1 client, written from scratch for Node.js. It is possible to inject CRLF sequences into request headers in undici in versions less than 5.7.1. A fix was released in version 5.8.0. Sanitizing all HTTP headers from untrusted sources to eliminate `\\r\\n` is a workaround for this issue.","cwe":["CWE-93 CWE-93: Improper Neutralization of CRLF Sequences ('CRLF Injection')"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","v":"3.1","score":5.3,"sev":"MEDIUM","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:N"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"poc","Automatable":"yes","Technical Impact":"partial"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"nodejs","product":"undici","versions":["affected < v5.7.1, >= v5.8.0"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/security/advisories/GHSA-3cvr-822r-rqcc","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://hackerone.com/reports/409943","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/releases/tag/v5.8.0","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://security.netapp.com/advisory/ntap-20220915-0002/","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]}],"vendors":["nodejs"]}
{"id":"CVE-2022-31151","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"GitHub_M","published":"2022-07-20T23:00:15.000Z","updated":"2025-04-22T17:48:20.472Z","title":"Uncleared cookies on cross-host/cross-origin redirect in undici","description":"Authorization headers are cleared on cross-origin redirect. However, cookie headers which are sensitive headers and are official headers found in the spec, remain uncleared. There are active users using cookie headers in undici. This may lead to accidental leakage of cookie to a 3rd-party site or a malicious attacker who can control the redirection target (ie. an open redirector) to leak the cookie to the 3rd party site. This was patched in v5.7.1. By default, this vulnerability is not exploitable. Do not enable redirections, i.e. `maxRedirections: 0` (the default).","cwe":["CWE-601 CWE-601: URL Redirection to Untrusted Site ('Open Redirect')"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","v":"3.1","score":3.7,"sev":"LOW","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:N"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"poc","Automatable":"no","Technical Impact":"partial"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"nodejs","product":"undici","versions":["affected < 5.7.1"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/security/advisories/GHSA-q768-x9m6-m9qp","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/issues/872","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://hackerone.com/reports/1635514","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://security.netapp.com/advisory/ntap-20220909-0006/","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]}],"vendors":["nodejs"]}
{"id":"CVE-2022-32210","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"hackerone","published":"2022-07-14T14:51:40.000Z","updated":"2024-08-03T07:32:56.020Z","description":"`Undici.ProxyAgent` never verifies the remote server's certificate, and always exposes all request & response data to the proxy. This unexpectedly means that proxies can MitM all HTTPS traffic, and if the proxy's URL is HTTP then it also means that nominally HTTPS requests are actually sent via plain-text HTTP between Undici and the proxy server.","cwe":["CWE-295 Improper Certificate Validation (CWE-295)"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"https://github.com/nodejs/undici","versions":["affected Fixed in version >= v5.5.1. Vulnerable between v4.8.2 and v5.5.0"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://hackerone.com/reports/1583680","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/security/advisories/GHSA-pgw7-wx7w-2w33","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]}],"vendors":["nodejs"]}
{"id":"CVE-2022-32212","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"hackerone","published":"2022-07-14T00:00:00.000Z","updated":"2025-04-30T22:24:44.217Z","description":"A OS Command Injection vulnerability exists in Node.js versions <14.20.0, <16.20.0, <18.5.0 due to an insufficient IsAllowedHost check that can easily be bypassed because IsIPAddress does not properly check if an IP address is invalid before making DBS requests allowing rebinding attacks.","cwe":["CWE-284 Improper Access Control - Generic (CWE-284)"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"NodeJS","product":"Node","defaultStatus":"unaffected","versions":["affected 4.0 <4.* (semver)","affected 5.0 <5.* (semver)","affected 6.0 <6.* (semver)","affected 7.0 <7.* (semver)","affected 8.0 <8.* (semver)","affected 9.0 <9.* (semver)","affected 10.0 <10.* (semver)","affected 11.0 <11.* (semver)","affected 12.0 <12.* (semver)","affected 13.0 <13.* (semver)","affected 14.0 <14.20.1 (semver)","affected 15.0 <15.* (semver)","affected 16.0 <16.17.1 (semver)","affected 17.0 <17.* (semver)","affected 18.0 <18.9.1 (semver)"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://hackerone.com/reports/1632921"}],"vendors":["nodejs"]}
